Depends: conky-all, waybar, swaybg, jq, python3, python3-gi, python3-gi-cairo, python3-cairo, python3-xlib, gir1.2-gtk-3.0, gir1.2-gtklayershell-0.1, gnome-control-center, gnome-settings-daemon, network-manager, network-manager-gnome, bluez, gnome-bluetooth, dconf-cli, gsettings-desktop-schemas, policykit-1-gnome, brightnessctl, playerctl, pulseaudio-utils, zenity, imagemagick, curl, libpam0g, libseat1, libinput10, libgbm1, libegl1, libxkbcommon0, xdg-desktop-portal, xdg-desktop-portal-wlr, pipewire, pipewire-pulse, wireplumber, slurp, wofi, plymouth, plymouth-themes, initramfs-tools
Recommends: ulauncher, nautilus, gnome-terminal, gnome-calculator, gnome-text-editor | gedit, gnome-software, fonts-inter
Description: Cosmoduck niri desktop (Ubuntu 22.04)
 Complete niri Wayland desktop setup for Ubuntu 22.04 (jammy): the niri
 compositor and supporting tools compiled from source (niri, Xwayland,
 xwayland-satellite, swaylock, swaync, libdisplay-info, libwayland-client
 1.23.1 for the Firefox scroll fix), the Cosmoduck GTK
 theme, a waybar top bar + macOS-style dock, swaync notifications, the
 conky Cosmoduck widget with an X11->layer-shell bridge to run it under
 niri, plus waybar toggles for the conky widget and lid keep-awake.
 .
 Binaries install under /usr/local. Per-user configuration is installed by
 running `cosmoduck-niri-setup` once per user. Designed for jammy, where
 niri is not packaged.
